Bench-Capon (2003) extends Dung's frameworks with *values*. Each
argument promotes a value (liberty, order, piety…), and each *audience*
ranks values. An attack only succeeds if the audience doesn't rank the
attacked argument's value above the attacker's.

So the same argument can win against one NPC and fail against another,
and the game never has to declare a value judgement true. Paper:
_Persuasion in practical argument using value-based argumentation
frameworks_, J. Logic and Computation 13(3).
